<title>FRANCE: Arthuis says must consolidate current FX levels.</title>
<headline>Arthuis says must consolidate current FX levels.</headline>
<dateline>LYON, France 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said on Wednesday that current exchange rates should be consolidated.</p>
<p>&quot;We must consolidate foreign exchange levels,&quot; Arthuis said when asked about the dollar and current international exchange rates.</p>
<p>He was speaking after a news conference at the end of a meeting between French and German finance ministers and central bank heads.</p>
<p>The franc was trading at 3.3725 per mark at 1332 GMT. The dollar was worth 1.7033 marks and 5.7470 francs.</p>
</text>
